Falsifies `pci::verification::read_bars_is_total_for_any_device`.

The defect: the BAR loop runs one slot past the end, `i <= 6` in place of `i < 6`. A header has
six BARs and both spellings look like "all six" at a glance; the 64-bit branch's `i += 2` already
makes the index arithmetic here non-obvious.

Expected to fail: the totality claim, as an out-of-bounds index on `out[i]` at `i == 6`. It
needs a device that answers the size probe with a non-zero mask on the seventh read, which is
exactly the arbitrary-response regime this harness quantifies over and nothing a fixture
supplies.

